    <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-f0d0110 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child">
        <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-39436d6 elementor-widget elementor-widget-n-accordion">
              <div class="e-n-accordion" aria-label="Accordion. Open links with Enter or Space, close with Escape, and navigate with Arrow Keys">
            <details id="e-n-accordion-item-6000" class="e-n-accordion-item" open="">
        <summary class="e-n-accordion-item-title" data-accordion-index="1" tabindex="0" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="e-n-accordion-item-6000">
          <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-header"><h3 class="e-n-accordion-item-title-text"> Q. What speed do most people prefer for audiobooks? </h3></span>
              <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-icon">
      <span class="e-opened"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-cross-circle"></i></span>
      <span class="e-closed"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-plus-circle"></i></span>
    </span>
            </summary>
        <div role="region" aria-labelledby="e-n-accordion-item-6000" class="elementor-element elementor-element-ff1174f e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child">
        <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-0dbce03 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor">
                  Most audiobook listeners find 1.5x speed the ideal starting point — it saves 33% of your listening time while maintaining excellent comprehension. Power users often settle at 2x after gradual practice. Use our audiobook speed calculator to instantly see how much time you save at any speed before you commit.                </div>
        </div>
          </details>
            <details id="e-n-accordion-item-6001" class="e-n-accordion-item">
        <summary class="e-n-accordion-item-title" data-accordion-index="2" tabindex="-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="e-n-accordion-item-6001">
          <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-header"><h3 class="e-n-accordion-item-title-text"> Q. How do I calculate audiobook listening time at a different speed? </h3></span>
              <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-icon">
      <span class="e-opened"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-cross-circle"></i></span>
      <span class="e-closed"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-plus-circle"></i></span>
    </span>
            </summary>
        <div role="region" aria-labelledby="e-n-accordion-item-6001" class="elementor-element elementor-element-8c8fb91 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child">
        <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-a309ccf elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor">
                  The audiobook listening time formula is simple: Adjusted Time = Original Duration ÷ Playback Speed. For example, a 10-hour audiobook at 1.5x playback speed takes 6 hours 40 minutes — saving you 3 hours 20 minutes. Our free audiobook speed calculator does this math instantly as you type.                 </div>
        </div>
          </details>
            <details id="e-n-accordion-item-6002" class="e-n-accordion-item">
        <summary class="e-n-accordion-item-title" data-accordion-index="3" tabindex="-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="e-n-accordion-item-6002">
          <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-header"><h3 class="e-n-accordion-item-title-text"> Q. Does listening to audiobooks at higher speeds hurt comprehension? </h3></span>
              <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-icon">
      <span class="e-opened"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-cross-circle"></i></span>
      <span class="e-closed"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-plus-circle"></i></span>
    </span>
            </summary>
        <div role="region" aria-labelledby="e-n-accordion-item-6002" class="elementor-element elementor-element-7f3cf86 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child">
        <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5ade0d1 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor">
                  Research shows audiobook listeners can maintain strong comprehension up to about 1.5x–2x playback speed when built up gradually. Above 2.5x, comprehension begins to drop for most people. The key is to increase your audiobook playback speed in small increments — try 1.1x for a week, then 1.25x, then 1.5x.                </div>
        </div>
          </details>
            <details id="e-n-accordion-item-6003" class="e-n-accordion-item">
