          <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-header"><h3 class="e-n-accordion-item-title-text"> Q. Which audiobook apps support speed control? </h3></span>
              <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-icon">
      <span class="e-opened"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-cross-circle"></i></span>
      <span class="e-closed"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-plus-circle"></i></span>
    </span>
            </summary>
        <div role="region" aria-labelledby="e-n-accordion-item-6003" class="elementor-element elementor-element-2e7d1c5 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child">
        <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-65db897 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor">
                  All major audiobook apps support playback speed control: Audible (0.5x–3.5x), Libby (0.5x–3x), Spotify Audiobooks (0.5x–3.5x), Apple Books (0.5x–2x), Google Play Books (0.5x–3x), and Kobo. Our audiobook speed calculator is app-agnostic — it works with any platform’s displayed runtime.                </div>
        </div>
          </details>
            <details id="e-n-accordion-item-6004" class="e-n-accordion-item">
        <summary class="e-n-accordion-item-title" data-accordion-index="5" tabindex="-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="e-n-accordion-item-6004">
          <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-header"><h3 class="e-n-accordion-item-title-text"> Q. How much time can I save by listening at 1.5x speed? </h3></span>
              <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-icon">
      <span class="e-opened"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-cross-circle"></i></span>
      <span class="e-closed"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-plus-circle"></i></span>
    </span>
            </summary>
        <div role="region" aria-labelledby="e-n-accordion-item-6004" class="elementor-element elementor-element-80524a9 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child">
        <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-5ab59d9 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor">
                  At 1.5x audiobook speed, you save exactly 33% of your listening time. A 10-hour audiobook takes 6h 40m. A 12-hour audiobook takes 8 hours. Over a year of regular listening, that adds up to dozens of extra hours — enough to finish several additional books. Use the calculator above to see your exact time saved.                 </div>
        </div>
          </details>
            <details id="e-n-accordion-item-6005" class="e-n-accordion-item">
        <summary class="e-n-accordion-item-title" data-accordion-index="6" tabindex="-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="e-n-accordion-item-6005">
          <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-header"><h3 class="e-n-accordion-item-title-text"> Q. Is the audiobook speed calculator free to use? </h3></span>
              <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-icon">
      <span class="e-opened"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-cross-circle"></i></span>
      <span class="e-closed"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-plus-circle"></i></span>
    </span>
            </summary>
        <div role="region" aria-labelledby="e-n-accordion-item-6005" class="elementor-element elementor-element-94f8fcf e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child">
        <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-002ae5d elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor">
                  Yes — completely free. The audiobook speed calculator works entirely in your browser with no installation, no sign-up, and no email required. There are no hidden costs, no premium tiers, and no ads inside the calculator tool itself.                 </div>
        </div>
          </details>
            <details id="e-n-accordion-item-6006" class="e-n-accordion-item">
        <summary class="e-n-accordion-item-title" data-accordion-index="7" tabindex="-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="e-n-accordion-item-6006">
          <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-header"><h3 class="e-n-accordion-item-title-text"> Q. Can I use this calculator for podcasts and lectures too? </h3></span>
              <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-icon">
      <span class="e-opened"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-cross-circle"></i></span>
      <span class="e-closed"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-plus-circle"></i></span>
    </span>
            </summary>
        <div role="region" aria-labelledby="e-n-accordion-item-6006" class="elementor-element elementor-element-ebb5197 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child">
        <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-e3adaef elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor">
                  Absolutely. The tool works for any audio content with a fixed duration — podcasts, university lectures, language courses, or sermon recordings. Just enter the total length and your playback speed to get your adjusted listening time instantly.                 </div>
        </div>
          </details>
            <details id="e-n-accordion-item-6007" class="e-n-accordion-item">
        <summary class="e-n-accordion-item-title" data-accordion-index="8" tabindex="-1" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="e-n-accordion-item-6007">
          <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-header"><h3 class="e-n-accordion-item-title-text"> Q. Does the calculator work on mobile devices? </h3></span>
              <span class="e-n-accordion-item-title-icon">
      <span class="e-opened"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-cross-circle"></i></span>
      <span class="e-closed"><i aria-hidden="true" class="icon icon-plus-circle"></i></span>
    </span>
            </summary>
        <div role="region" aria-labelledby="e-n-accordion-item-6007" class="elementor-element elementor-element-bb472b2 e-con-full e-flex e-con e-child">
        <div class="elementor-element elementor-element-8f6cc07 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor">
                  Yes. The audiobook speed calculator is fully responsive and optimized for all screen sizes. The touch-friendly slider, large tap-to-adjust spinners, and speed preset buttons work perfectly on both iOS and Android devices.                </div>
        </div>
